## Limits

State only what the module note supports. Candidates: sigma_hat
calibrates from the observed log times with censored rows at their
censoring values, so the lambda prior is calibrated on a biased scale
and no correction is derived; the refresh-then-Gaussian-sweep scan is
stated valid by the shared censoring argument, and the written proof
under the frozen min-max map of ln t is not in the repository; under a
variance ensemble the truncated draw's variance is s^2(x_i), and the
heteroscedastic AFT model has no calibration entry; the tobit offset
and the interval model's equal-bounds rule are operational, not
derived; the `abart` comparison is informational, since the priors
differ.

